I am thinking that we could instead of killing the Wizard, drain him
down to something like 8 level. This would prevent him from doing
anything nasty. I guess it will take a long time to drain him to such
levels, but it may be usefull. Can anybody comment if this will make
the end-game any simpler. I would think that he will not be able to
cast summon nasties, which is the major trouble. He can't even cast
touch of death. And due to the low level you can simply ignore him, as
the chance for him to succeed in stealing will be very low, he will
just keep on missing. For getting the book polymorph into a nymph. It
will be nice to ascend without killing the wizard ;-).

The other idea I had was because some monsters covet the Amulet, and
many of them will follow you. If we find any monster like this, we
could throw the Amulet to the monster, which will promptly pick it up,
and then when it comes near you to attack, just use a level teleport. I
am expecting that the monster will teleport with me. Does this loophole
exist, I haven't seen anybody use it.



